    "body": "## Problem\n\n69aa33d890 (#31563) added Tree-sitter capture-based skipping so that matching from code ignores delimiters inside strings and comments when legacy syntax groups are unavailable. The new branch bypassed the existing exception that disables skipping when the cursor starts inside one of those regions. The Lua rewrite in 523e679ead (#39625) preserved this structure. Consequently, matching from inside a Tree-sitter string or comment can miss its pair or highlight a delimiter in surrounding code.\n\n## Solution\n\nApply the initial-position exception to both syntax backends. Matching from code still uses the same capture-based skip predicate to ignore strings and comments, preserving the goal of #31563. When matching starts inside a skipped region, disable skipping as legacy syntax does. Extend the existing other-window test to cover code containing a string with an unmatched delimiter, plus pairs inside strings and comments in both directions.",
    "closed_at": null,
